<p>President Donald Trump said on February 27 that the United States is holding talks with Cuba, and he suggested the process could lead to a possible “friendly takeover” of the island. He said Secretary of State Marco Rubio is negotiating “at a high level” with the Cuban government. Several outlets framed the remarks around Cuba’s deepening economic strains and shortages, with Trump saying the government has “no money”. Other coverage pointed to rising tensions between Washington and Havana, and Al Jazeera tied the moment to US pressure on Cuba’s fuel situation. The language is unusually blunt, but direct talks still leave room for a diplomatic opening — depending on what negotiators pursue next.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/eIxrQxgIi5I9JkVBqtH6UGlUGRw-hKms6dUb6Mkhe3hEyOi67zPQ8-s7pjPbHO3hmuT718GglZ5n5-bcOcIEDAUDNJwf6ofkSfRIBOPiX2rhRwGcJAuNLbuc_QeydLGJkFgCVrCYWgtPLmyDAIqE1NxSn65UgASTtP3qqTcJgr-dqdZvHuHhoqVYoU7JNsWSfzxk9ag44zebxqQVv7RMBwAz1SXuMeLeJUXm6Ekn7F8SkgX5i0ho4H7LiBUzSqh_N4UmH8Xj2izqaw_i4g' alt='President Donald Trump speaks with reporters before departing on Marine One from the South Lawn of the White House on Friday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Where he spoke: Trump made the comments to reporters as he left the White House for Texas.</li><li>Exiles angle: Trump said a “friendly takeover” could be “very positive” for people who were “expelled, or worse, from Cuba” and now live in the United States, adding that some want to return.</li><li>How he characterized Cuba: The Straits Times said Trump described Cuba as a failing nation that needs change.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: He said the Cuban government is “talking with us” and floated the idea of a “friendly takeover.” He added it could be “very positive” for people “expelled, or worse, from Cuba” who now live in the US and want to go back. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3344941/trump-says-us-discussing-friendly-takeover-cuba-theyre-big-trouble'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera framing: Al Jazeera said the comments came amid a US fuel blockade and reported that Trump portrayed Cuba as seeking US help. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/27/trump-suggests-a-friendly-takeover-of-cuba-amid-us-fuel-blockade'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>The Guardian context: The Guardian said tensions between Washington and Havana have hit new highs and tied the moment to the capture of Venezuela’s Nicolás Maduro. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/27/trump-cuba-regime-change'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>RT account: RT said Washington has tightened economic pressure after a US raid in Venezuela, and reported that Trump portrayed Cuba as nearing collapse while in contact with Washington. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633152-trump-cuba-friendly-takeover/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-suggests-u-s-could-have-friendly-takeover-of-cuba'>Trump suggests U.S. could have &#x27;friendly takeover of Cuba&#x27;</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/02/27/trump-floats-a-friendly-takeover-of-cuba-says-talks-are-under-way-with-havana'>Trump floats a “friendly takeover” of Cuba, says talks are under way with Havana</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3344941/trump-says-us-discussing-friendly-takeover-cuba-theyre-big-trouble'>Trump says US discussing ‘friendly takeover’ of Cuba: ‘they’re in big trouble’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/they-have-no-money-donald-trump-hints-at-friendly-takeover-of-cuba-11148170#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;They Have No Money&quot;: Trump Hints At &quot;Friendly Takeover&quot; Of Cuba</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/27/trump-cuba-regime-change'>Trump suggests US could carry out ‘friendly takeover’ of Cuba</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a hr